  "aboutParagraphs": [
    "Blue Ribbon Pines is the crown jewel of Minnesota disc golf — 27 holes of open-and-wooded design with ponds, doglegs, and risk-reward decisions on almost every tee. Timmy Gill and Steve Beckman built it in 2006, and it's been a top-ranked destination ever since.",
    "It's pay to play at $8 a day, with a pro shop on site — the kind of course people drive across the state for. The mix of big open drives and tight wooded lines keeps 27 holes from ever feeling repetitive.",
    "Bring a full bag and a full day. This is the round Twin Cities players measure their season against."
