  "signatureHoleDescription": "Hole 18 is the longest at Blue Ribbon at 624 feet — a par 4 that combines everything the course does well: a big drive, a placed second shot, and water close enough to make you think. It's the hole that sums up why people drive across Minnesota to play here.",
  "localTips": "Pay to play ($8/day) with a pro shop on site — worth every dollar. All 27 holes is a full day, so start early. The ponds and doglegs reward risk-takers and punish the careless; bring your whole bag.",
